From: Simone Rota <simone.rota16@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:51:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] fix(EDDI): duplicated local variables start with the
 content of the original ones

The code generated for a bit-field assignment loads the whole word, updates
some bits and stores it back: the consistency check on the store compared the
uninitialized (different) bits of the two copies of the variable, a false data
corruption that depends on the stack contents. At the beginning of each
hardened function the content of every local variable is copied into its
duplicate.
---
 passes/ASPIS.h  |  2 ++
 passes/EDDI.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

